cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this work, please cite it as below."
title: "uttt-zero: an AlphaZero-style agent for Ultimate Tic-Tac-Toe, built to analyse the game"
abstract: >-
  A single-PC AlphaZero-style agent for Ultimate Tic-Tac-Toe under CodinGame
  rules (closed boards, free moves, most-boards decision), trained by self-play
  and used as an instrument to establish what is true about the game: opening
  value, the worth of a free move, when games become decided, and what the
  network computes internally. Every claim carries its level, effect size,
  confidence interval, the networks it held across, and the tool that produced
  it.
authors:
